course: dictionary
lesson: 14435
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The sentence tells you which meaning the author wants. «The paddler steered the canoe down the river.» The clues are canoe and river, so a paddler here is a person who paddles a boat.
explain: «The little children were paddlers at the beach, splashing with bare feet in the shallow waves.» The clues are beach, bare feet and shallow waves, so a paddler here is a person wading in shallow water. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: does it still make sense?
explain: The two meanings are about different activities, a boat on a river and feet in the sea, but the word is the same. When you meet a word with more than one meaning, look at the words around it and ask which activity is happening.
fact: A paddler is a person who paddles a canoe, kayak or paddleboard.
fact: In the UK and Ireland, a paddler is also a person, often a child, walking in shallow water at the seaside or in a paddling pool.
fact: «Paddle» is the verb: you paddle a boat, or you paddle in shallow water.
fact: Water safety tip: paddlers should wear a life jacket and watch out for tides.
fact: «Paddler» is a noun, and its plural is «paddlers».
exercise: «The paddlers raced their kayaks across the lake.» What is a paddler here? | A person walking in shallow water at the seaside | A bird that lives near water | *A person who paddles a kayak | A type of wet sand
exercise: «Toddlers were paddlers in the paddling pool, splashing with bare feet.» What does paddler mean here? | A kind of swimming costume | A person rowing a canoe on a river | A pool cleaner | *A person walking in shallow water
exercise: Which safety rule should a paddler on a river follow? | *Wear a life jacket | Swim out as far as possible | Take off all your clothes | Ignore the weather
test: «Mia, a paddler on the lake, wore her life jacket all day.» What does paddler mean here? | A type of boat engine | A lake monster | *A person who paddles a kayak | A person walking in shallow water at the seaside
test: What is the verb form of paddler? | padded | paddling pool | paddleboard | *paddle
exam: «Before the tide came in, the paddlers at the seaside were told to leave the shallow water.» What does paddler mean here? | A person who paddles a canoe on the sea | *A person walking in shallow water at the seaside | A type of tide | A lifeguard on a boat
